      "caption": "Woodward's lactam (indole + E ring joined through nitrogen) + phosphoryl chloride",
      "learnerPrompt": "Turn the lactam C=O into a leaving group: let its oxygen attack phosphorus.",
      "hintTiers": [
        "An amide oxygen is the most nucleophilic atom of an amide (think of where amides are protonated). Phosphorus in POCl₃ carries three chlorides that can leave.",
        "The lactam oxygen bonds to phosphorus and a chloride leaves. The nitrogen lone pair can then push in to make a C=N⁺ iminium ion, with the C=O π pair moving onto oxygen. Two arrows are enough; four give the drawing used next.",
        "Lactam oxygen lone pair → new O–P bond; P–Cl bond → lone pair on chloride; nitrogen lone pair → C=N π bond; C=O π bond → lone pair on oxygen."
      ],
