      "explanationAfterStep": "The lactam oxygen attacks phosphorus and a chloride leaves. The product is drawn as an iminium ion, the nitrogen lone pair pushing in: the O–P(O)Cl₂ group has turned the unreactive amide C=O into an electrophilic C=N⁺ with a leaving group. A secondary amide would go on to a nitrilium ion; this lactam's nitrogen has no hydrogen, so the iminium ion itself is attacked."
