  "mechanismSummary": "Woodward's lactam joins the indole half (from 6-methoxytryptamine) to the E-ring half through its nitrogen. Phosphoryl chloride turns the lactam C=O into an iminium ion carrying a dichlorophosphate leaving group; the indole attacks it at its free 2-position (an intramolecular electrophilic aromatic substitution) to close ring C; chloride removes a proton to restore the aromatic indole; and the nitrogen pushes out dichlorophosphate to leave a dihydro-β-carbolinium ion. The E-ring substituents (CO₂Me, OMe, OAc) and the aryl OMe take no part and are drawn as labels; stereocentres are not drawn.",
